{
  "_comment": "Roof assemblies (kind 'roof'). The driver is a closed horizontal boundary = the plate line (outside face of the wall framing); base_offset = plate height. Settings (any of them can also be a driver param): shape flat | shed | gable, pitch (x in 12), overhang (eave, plate line to fascia face), rake, ridge (long | short | degrees), flip (shed: high side), wall_depth / wall_ext / wall_int (bearing walls: framing depth, layers outside / inside it), trim {...} (mindcanvas/roofs/shape.py TRIM: fascia, sub-fascia, soffit + vent + nailer, drip edge, gutter, rake board, barge, lookouts, bird blocks, ridge cap). 'layers' = the roof-plane stack TOP -> BOTTOM around the 'rafters' layer (system wood | metal: the one-line swap; rafter; spacing; cavity_fill; fill_depth). Layer options: taper (in/ft), eave_membrane, region, shingles: exposure, tip. 'ceiling' = optional attic ceiling stack (component 'joists' = ceiling joists beside the rafters).",

